      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-340844",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform $L{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}$ using the smoothness property. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $f(t)={e}^{4t}$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{\u2033}(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={{field-3}},\\,s>4.\n$$"
